<article class="env-proposition" id="B1A74B">
       
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/B1A74B">Proposition <span data-tag="B1A74B">6.3.1.7</span>.</a><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
Let $p: X \rightarrow S$ be a Cartesian fibration of simplicial sets, classified by a map $\chi : S^{op} \rightarrow \widehat{\Cat }_{\infty }$. Then $p$ is a topos fibration if and only if $\chi $ factors through $\RGeom \subseteq \widehat{\Cat }_{\infty }$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
Let $p: X \rightarrow S$ be a coCartesian fibration of simplicial sets, classified by a map $\chi : S \rightarrow \widehat{\Cat }_{\infty }$. Then $p$ is a topos fibration if and only if $\chi $ factors through $\LGeom \subseteq \widehat{\Cat }_{\infty }$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
